tchedAt":"2026-10-30T16:32:22+00:00","id":"hr10582-119","introducedDate":"2026-09-24","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-09-24","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"laws":[],"number":"10582","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Taxation","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"M001224","district":1,"fullName":"Rep. Moran, Nathaniel [R-TX-1]","party":"R","state":"TX"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2026-09-24","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Motion Picture, Television, and Entertainment Revitalization Act</strong></p><p>This bill establishes a federal business tax credit for a percentage of the compensation paid for services performed in the United States related to a qualified film or television production. (Conditions and exceptions apply.)</p><p>The bill defines a <em>qualified film or television production</em> as any production that is</p><ul><li>a feature film, television pilot, or television season;</li><li>produced in the ordinary course of business for commercial purposes;</li><li>capitalized;</li><li>completed during the tax year with more than $1 million in total costs; and</li><li>filmed in the United States for 75% of the photography days.</li></ul><p>Under the bill, various types of programming are not a qualified film or television production, including news programs, live sporting events, and programming intended primarily for social media platforms.</p><p>The amount of the tax credit is 20% (base tax credit percentage) of the compensation paid for services performed in the United States related to a qualified film or television production. The base tax credit percentage increases by increments of 5% (up to a maximum tax credit percentage of 30%) if</p><ul><li>at least 30% of the production is filmed in a federally declared disaster area or rural qualified opportunity zone,</li><li>the production is independently produced, or</li><li>the production meets certain multi-state or increased domestic production requirements.</li></ul><p>Special rules apply to animations, visual effects productions, and post-production activities.</p><p>Finally, the tax credit may be transferred to an unrelated third party in exchange for cash.</p>","updateDate":"2026-10-06T14:19:57Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Motion Picture, Television, and Entertainment Revitalization Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-10-30T08:06:37Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-10-30T08:06:37Z"}
